Z||000000||Dan010||10-07-2001||09:47 PM||||Searched thru this forum about this subject,<BR>found some bought at pep boys, Fiero store<BR>ect. .<BR> What is the difference between these and auto zone, or others<BR>Have not checked the one on my 86gt yet, but <BR>dont like the feel or sound when shifting between drive and reverse, and reverse to drive slowly of course.<BR> After reading your post, could be tthese and or the dog bone, am thinking of replacing all, has almost 90k now.<BR>Thanks, you all have been very helpfull and<BR>patient with my questions.<BR>Dan||||reg||1
Z||000001||2birds||10-07-2001||10:01 PM||||The transaxle and under the timing chain cover motor mounts are pretty much the same, no matter who makes them, unless you spring the $$$ for the poly mounts talked about here once in a while.  All three were under $10 each, GM parts probably a good bit more, but no better, IMHO.  The Sealed Power mounts I got from Discount Auto didn't fit perfectly (studs were about 1/4" off).  The ones I got from Autozone fit perfectly, and were about a buck cheaper.  <BR>I haven't been able to find an OEM style dogbone anywhere but the GM dealers.  Lots of people make poly bushings for the stock dogbone, or whole new bones with poly bushings already installed.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||10-07-2001||11:20 PM||||I can appreciate why people like poly, but if you replace all of the rubber in the cradle and suspension with *new* rubber, the result is amazing. Tight and quiet.<P>Also, the vibration dampener (looks like a small shock) from the V6 engine to the cradle has a tremendous affect on the feel of the car especially during accel and deceleration. The rubber bushings wear out. GM stopped making them this year. I'm looking for a replacement. Frankly, I think there is a spring in there rather than a shock. I took one from an X body and was able to get the sleeve through the rubber (smaller diameter). What a difference.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-08-2001||09:20 PM||||used polly motor mounts before.... haaated 'um. <P>I'd do the cradel in polly again but never motor/tranny mounts.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
